this contains the old Monterey grid using SRTM 1.5 as bathymetry, which looked bad
the new grid uses a high resolution DEM from NOAA that is 1/3 arc sec (~10 m horizontal
resolution)

https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/metadata/geoportal/rest/metadata/item/gov.noaa.ngdc.mgg.dem:3545/html

1/3 arc second ~ 10 m resolution
MHW referenced
https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/datums.html?id=9413450
Need to subtract 0.55 m to DEM to get mean sea level for ROMS

